		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Game Simulation Engineer - US, WA]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=939#p939"><![CDATA[
We are passionate about building simulation titles based in real-world representations that provide entertainment and educational experiences. Sound challenging? The Aces Studio has built the Flight Simulator, Combat Flight Simulator, and Train Simulator products and we are looking for a simulation engineer to join us. Potential candidates need to have strong skills in basic engineering, math modeling, and programming physical systems and vehicles for real-time simulation. It is essential that you have the ability to generate rigid body dynamics through Newtonian physics and 6-DOF equations of motion, posses an understanding of feedback control systems, and be able to design and integrate new technologies within existing code bases. Additional areas of responsibility may include: implementation of vehicle panels and instrumentation systems, audio, effect triggers, and low-level AI controllers for the vehicles. <br>Education and experience requirements: a BS (or equivalent) degree in Computer Science or Computer Engineering; strong debugging skills; at least 3 years of C/C++ development experience. Previous game industry development experience is preferred. <br><br>To submit your resume, please use this link:<br><a href="http://members.microsoft.com/careers/search/details.aspx?JobID=11DA7D3F-EB07-4823-8B47-45D75B2F33F1&amp;start=1&amp;interval=10" class="postlink">http://members.microsoft.com/careers/se ... nterval=10</a><br><br>For questions, please send a mail to <a href="mailto:nickco.nospamplease@microsoft.com">nickco.nospamplease@microsoft.com</a>.<br>(remove ".nospamplease")<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=489">ncoder</a> — Wed Apr 26, 2006 4:47 pm</p><hr />
